ication/issues/comments/5580666403","html_url":"https://github.com/eclipse-score/communication/issues/782#issuecomment-5580666403","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eclipse-score/communication/issues/782","id":5580666403,"node_id":"IC_kwDOODov5M8AAAABTKI2Iw","user":{"login":"bharatGoswami8","id":228470805,"node_id":"U_kgDODZ4wFQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228470805?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bharatGoswami8","html_url":"https://github.com/bharatGoswami8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bharatGoswami8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bharatGoswami8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bharatGoswami8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bharatGoswami8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bharatGoswami8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bharatGoswami8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bharatGoswami8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bharatGoswami8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bharatGoswami8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-08T06:56:33Z","updated_at":"2026-09-08T06:56:33Z","body":"Hello @hskang-amelia ,\n\n> First — on the sync/async bridge strategy: For milestone 1, can we just wrap the synchronous LoLa call in an already-resolved future? Or do you want real async dispatch from the start? Because issue 767 might actually go away if we do real async instead of blocking a thread.\n\nIssue 767 is related to the C++ side implementation, or more specifically, the concrete backend implementation. Ideally, the issue should be addressed in the underlying implementation first, and then we can introduce the appropriate API or bridge-layer changes on top of that. Resolving it only at the Rust layer would not address the actual root cause.\n\nIn the current Rust library design, we have a runtime layer that is backend-specific. This runtime layer invokes the bridge APIs, where the FFI calls map directly to the corresponding C++ implementations.\n\n> And second — on scope: Is E2E protection for Rust Methods and Fields part of 782’s first milestone, or should that be a separate issue? I searched the repo and there’s no E2E issue at all right now.\n\nRegarding E2E protection, we have not considered it so far, even for the existing Event implementation in rust side. it is something we should enable eventually. Since there is currently no tracking item for this work, it would be good to create a separate improvement ticket scoped to the Rust APIs.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eclipse-score/communication/issues/comments/5580666403/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"bharatGoswami8","id":228470805,"node_id":"U_kgDODZ4wFQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228470805?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bharatGoswami8","html_url":"https://github.com/bharatGoswami8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bharatGoswami8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bharatGoswami8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bharatGoswami8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bharatGoswami8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bharatGoswami8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bharatGoswami8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bharatGoswami8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bharatGoswami8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bharatGoswami8/received_eve